<title>SINGAPORE: IME expects improvements in 1997/98.</title>
<headline>IME expects improvements in 1997/98.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Retail, wholesale and entertainment company IMM Multi-Entertainment (IME) Ltd said on Monday it expected to show an improvement for the current financial year as some of the losses incurred in the previous year were non-recurring.</p>
<p>The company said in the announcement of its full year results ended February 28, 1997 that the losses were due to fixed asset write-offs and new start-ups and closure of unprofitable outlets.</p>
<p>IME reported a loss of Singapore $1.07 million for the year compared to a previous S$2.08 million profit.  </p>
<p>The company said turnover rose to S$227.81 million from S$182.62 million due to the opening of two new retail outlets by its Yaohan Best Electrical chain of stores.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3080)</p>
